      "pronunciationText": "Here's how the practical runs. It follows your school's risk assessment, with solutions your teacher has approved, usually metal chlorides. You'll need a Bunsen burner with the air hole open, giving a hot blue flame, and a nichrome wire loop, which doesn't colour the flame itself. Clean the loop as your school's method says, then heat it until the flame shows no colour. Then dip the loop in a solution, hold it at the edge of the blue flame, and record the colour straight away. Clean the loop, and repeat with the next solution.",
