      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "So what does a colour tell you? It tells you which metal is likely to be present, because the colour comes from the metal's electrons. It doesn't tell you the rest of the compound. Sodium chloride and sodium nitrate both give the same yellow-orange flame. The chloride or nitrate part doesn't change the colour. And because you watch and record it yourself, it's primary data.",
