      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "If you said lithium, you might be right. But strontium gives a very similar red. By eye, you can't reliably tell them apart. Calcium's orange-red is close as well. Colours are hard to describe, too. One person's crimson is another person's scarlet. So a colour alone can point to more than one metal.",
