      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Some metals give no useful colour at all. Magnesium compounds, for example, give out mostly ultraviolet light, which you can't see. The flame just stays blue. And a flame test says nothing about how much of a metal is there. A faint colour might mean a dilute solution, or just a poor dip.",
