      "fullScaleSamples": 0,
      "silencesAtLeast1_5s": [],
      "lowScoreWords": [],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "You've met the cause already, with hydrogen's line spectrum. The flame's heat gives the metal's electrons energy, lifting them to higher energy levels. As they drop back, they give out photons, with energies set by the gaps between that metal's own levels. A flame shows several of these at once, and your eye blends them into a single colour. So each metal gives its own colour.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
