      "lowScoreWords": [],
      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Each step has a reason. That first test, with a clean loop and no sample, is a blank. It shows what the loop and flame give on their own, so any colour you see later comes from the sample. A blue flame matters, because the yellow flame you get with the air hole closed would hide the colours. Cleaning between tests stops one sample colouring the next. And testing each solution more than once checks that your observation is reliable. For safety, wear safety glasses, tie back long hair, and remember the loop stays hot. Some of these compounds are toxic, so wash your hands afterwards.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
